  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing the sum of all pairwise differences between outcomes of the two lotteries, which is a structural, mathematical comparison independent of the individual's wealth or current balance. The individual, however, based their reasoning on the perceived severity of losses in relation to their personal financial situation and the worst-case outcome. They did not mention any comparison of outcome differences, nor did they reference the mathematical structure of the lotteries. Their justification is based on personal loss aversion and worst-case scenarios, not on the sum of pairwise differences. Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual applied the decision reason. The information considered (current balance, worst-case loss) and the justification (relative severity of loss) are unrelated to the formal rule of the decision reason. The decision reason was not used.",
